"""
Handoff weight measurement (David, Oct 26, step 6): MEASUREMENT ONLY, the result is not used in control.

    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/handoff_weight_measure.py --liquid 0.10 --out data/handoff_weight/<name>

The normal layout's pipeline episode with the beaker's liquid mass set to --liquid (glass 0.10 kg as now), changed here in the test harness only (load_task's beaker_cfg; task_config is untouched). At each
handoff point the arm's still window is found and the hand load fitted (src/weight_estimate.py):
  * pick handoff: the end of the pick (the lift, the beaker held in the air); the arm stays there;
  * place handoff: the end of the place module (after the release, the back-off and the return to the zombie pose, the hand empty); the arm stays there. (The place module goes straight from the
    back-off to the return home without stopping, so the arm is never still at the back-off: an extra reading at the end of BACK is taken with the module's own, looser settled speed.)
Still: every joint of the arm below STILL_SPEED for the whole WINDOW; the reading is the mean over that window. The measurement reads only angles, speeds, the applied motor torque and the arm's own
gravity torque; the true mass (body_mass of the beaker) is read AFTER the run, for the answer key.
Slip: the beaker's position in the pad frame at the start of the lift against its largest change until the release (at 0.30 kg: did it move in the grip).
"""

import argparse
import gc
import json
import os
import sys
from collections import deque
from pathlib import Path

PROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))
sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT / "experiments"))
